  "bio_settings": "Settings",
  "bio_settingsHint": "Set up biometrics in your device settings.",
  "help_start_title": "Getting started",
  "help_start_1Title": "Dashboard",
  "help_start_1Body": "A countdown to the wedding, shortcuts to sections and the key figures. You arrange the tiles yourself — hide the ones you don't use.",
  "help_start_2Title": "Where do I start?",
  "help_start_2Body": "A suggested order for planning the wedding. Tick off completed steps and the bar shows your progress. You can open it from Settings at any time — the list is shared by everyone organising the wedding.",
  "help_start_3Title": "Guide vs. Help",
  "help_start_3Body": "The guide walks you through the app step by step and highlights things on screen. Help (this screen) is an encyclopedia of features, for when you're after a specific answer.",
  "help_guests_title": "Guests",
  "help_guests_1Title": "Guest list",
  "help_guests_1Body": "Add invitees and manage their details. Every guest can have a companion — add them on the guest's entry rather than as a separate guest, so the totals in the summary add up.",
  "help_guests_2Title": "Guest details",
  "help_guests_2Body": "Everything useful for planning: diet, allergies, age, whether they need accommodation and transport, notes. These details also drive the Budget calculations and the assignments in Accommodation.",
  "help_guests_3Title": "Guest summary",
  "help_guests_3Body": "The totals in one place: invited, confirmed, children, diets. Check them before you talk to the venue — catering is agreed on this basis.",
  "help_guests_4Title": "RSVPs",
  "help_guests_4Body": "There are two sources: entries you add yourself in the panel, and replies guests send from the guest zone. You'll find the latter under Settings → Guest interactions → RSVP. Each guest sends one reply and can update it themselves if plans change.",
  "help_budget_title": "Budget",
  "help_budget_1Title": "One source of truth — the most important rule",
  "help_budget_1Body": "An item added under Vendors, Gifts or Honeymoon shows up in the Budget automatically, labelled „added in…\". Edit it where it was created — that way nothing is counted twice and you don't have to keep two lists in sync.",
  "help_budget_2Title": "Budget summary",
  "help_budget_2Body": "Your limit against your spending, what's left to allocate, and every payment and deadline in one place.",
  "help_budget_3Title": "Venue and catering",
  "help_budget_3Body": "You enter a per-person rate and the app works out the cost from the number of guests. You can count in staff (photographer, band) separately, children at a different rate, and guests not yet assigned to tables. Set the venue's guaranteed minimum too, if your contract has one.",
  "help_budget_4Title": "Expenses",
  "help_budget_4Body": "All other costs, grouped into categories. You edit the categories under Settings → Configuration.",
  "help_budget_5Title": "Alcohol and drinks",
  "help_budget_5Body": "Types, quantities and prices — alcohol and soft drinks kept apart. Handy when deciding what you bring yourselves and what comes from the venue.",
  "help_budget_6Title": "Honeymoon",
  "help_budget_6Body": "Counted separately from the wedding costs so it doesn't distort the reception budget — but its payments appear in the Summary alongside the rest.",
  "help_budget_7Title": "Instalments and payment dates",
  "help_budget_7Body": "Break a vendor or expense down into instalments with dates. Upcoming deadlines show up in the Budget summary and on the dashboard.",
  "help_room_title": "Seating plan",
  "help_room_1Title": "Arranging the room",
  "help_room_1Body": "Turn on „Edit plan\" to drag tables and objects around and resize them. Outside edit mode the plan is for browsing and seating guests — it's harder to move something by accident.",
  "help_room_2Title": "Seating guests at tables",
  "help_room_2Body": "Drag a guest onto a seat at a table. Unseated guests are listed separately — keep an eye on them, as they may count towards the catering cost depending on your Budget settings.",
  "help_room_3Title": "Staff tables",
  "help_room_3Body": "Mark tables for the photographer, band or crew separately — they have their own catering rate and don't mix with the guest list.",
  "help_schedule_title": "Schedule and tasks",
  "help_schedule_1Title": "Running order",
  "help_schedule_1Body": "Programme items with times, a category and a place. It's the single most important document of the day — the photographer, the band and the venue staff will all want it.",
  "help_schedule_2Title": "Private item",
  "help_schedule_2Body": "An item marked private does NOT reach the guest zone. Use it for logistics: „florist arrives\", „settle up with the venue\".",
  "help_schedule_3Title": "Map link for guests",
  "help_schedule_3Body": "You can add a map link to an item and separately decide whether guests see it. Without ticking that option the link stays just for you.",
  "help_schedule_4Title": "Checklist",
  "help_schedule_4Body": "Things to tick off before and during the wedding — separate from Tasks, because it's for quick „done / not done\".",
  "help_schedule_5Title": "Tasks and links between them",
  "help_schedule_5Body": "You can assign a task to a person and link it to an expense, a vendor or a gift. That way one screen tells you what's left to do and what it costs.",
  "help_vendors_title": "Vendors, transport, accommodation",
  "help_vendors_1Title": "Vendors",
  "help_vendors_1Body": "Contacts, contract amounts, payment statuses and instalments. A vendor's amount goes into the Budget automatically — don't add it a second time as an expense.",
  "help_vendors_2Title": "Transport",
  "help_vendors_2Body": "Routes, vehicles and passenger assignments. The „needs transport\" flag comes from the guest's details.",
  "help_vendors_3Title": "Accommodation",
  "help_vendors_3Body": "Places, rooms and bookings for guests. Like transport, it uses the flags from the guest details.",
  "help_guestZone_title": "Guest zone",
  "help_guestZone_1Title": "Guest link and QR code",
  "help_guestZone_1Body": "Settings → „Guest link and QR\". A guest opens the page without signing in and without installing anything. This is the code you print on invitations or leave on the tables.",
  "help_guestZone_2Title": "Join code (guest account)",
  "help_guestZone_2Body": "A six-character code for a guest who wants the wedding on their own account. Verification is threefold: the code, the wedding date and the surname — the code alone isn't enough, since it's often out in the open.",
  "help_guestZone_3Title": "Section visibility for guests",
  "help_guestZone_3Body": "You decide which sections guests see and for how long (FROM/TO dates). You also choose what happens outside that window: an „available from…\" message, or hiding the tile entirely. Typically: turn RSVP on right away, the gallery only on the wedding day.",
  "help_guestZone_4Title": "Guest interactions and moderation",
  "help_guestZone_4Body": "Settings → „Guest interactions\". One place gathers RSVPs, guest book entries, advice, photos, music suggestions and game scores. You can delete any entry with a single tap.",
  "help_guestZone_5Title": "What a guest cannot see",
  "help_guestZone_5Body": "The budget, the full guest list, vendors, the seating plan and tasks are off limits to guests — and not merely hidden in the interface: they have no technical access to that data.",
  "help_media_title": "Photos and music",
  "help_media_1Title": "Gallery",
  "help_media_1Body": "A shared album: guests upload photos from their phones, you see everything in the panel and can delete anything you'd rather not keep.",
  "help_media_2Title": "Music and guest suggestions",
  "help_media_2Body": "You build the wedding playlist and guests send in song suggestions. Only you see the suggestions — there's no public list and no voting. Mark each one „We'll play it\" or „Declined\".",
  "help_games_title": "Games and keepsakes",
  "help_games_1Title": "Quiz, True/False, Guess the photo",
  "help_games_1Body": "Add questions and switch the game on with the „active\" toggle. Guests play on their own phones and the score comes to you. There's no public ranking — nobody is compared with anyone else.",
  "help_games_2Title": "Photo challenges",
  "help_games_2Body": "A list of photo tasks with points. A guest sends one photo per challenge; a new one replaces the old.",
  "help_games_3Title": "Wedding Bingo",
  "help_games_3Body": "You can type the bingo squares in by hand or generate them from the schedule. Boards print to PDF, and guests can also play on their phones.",
  "help_games_4Title": "Keepsakes",
  "help_games_4Body": "The guest book, advice for the couple, the time capsule and the guest map. The capsule is private — only you read it.",
  "help_roles_title": "Roles and access",
  "help_roles_1Title": "The owner has the final say",
  "help_roles_1Body": "The couple's account outranks everything. Only the owner adds people, issues invitations and can revoke anyone's access — the planner included.",
  "help_roles_2Title": "Co-organiser",
  "help_roles_2Body": "Best man, mum, a close friend — the full panel with no expiry date. They can't add further people, though; that stays with the owner.",
  "help_roles_3Title": "Planner and the expiry date",
  "help_roles_3Body": "You can give a planner access with an expiry date. After that date the wedding disappears from their list. Access can be blocked and restored at any time, as often as you like.",
  "help_roles_4Title": "How to add a planner or co-organiser — step by step",
  "help_roles_4Body": "Settings → „People and access\" → „Add person\". Pick the role (Co-organiser or Planner), and for a planner set an access expiry date. Then you have two routes: give their e-mail address (they must already have an account in the app) or generate an invitation code and pass it on however you like. An invitation adds someone to THIS wedding only — with several weddings each needs its own invitation.",
  "help_roles_5Title": "How the invitation code works",
  "help_roles_5Body": "The code is single-use and tied to one wedding and one role. Whoever gets it creates an account (or signs in to an existing one), then picks „I have an invitation code (co-organiser / planner)\" on the wedding list and enters it. Once used, the code stops working — generate a new one for the next person. This is a different route from the guest code, which guests use to join the guest zone.",
  "help_roles_6Title": "The planner's access expiry date",
  "help_roles_6Body": "You set the date when inviting and change it later on the people list. Once it passes, the wedding disappears from the planner's list and they lose access to the data — without anything being deleted on your side. The date can be pushed back, and access blocked and restored as often as you need. A co-organiser has no expiry date.",
  "help_roles_7Title": "Revoking access",
  "help_roles_7Body": "On the „People and access\" list every person has a block and a remove action. Blocking keeps them on the list (you can unblock them); removing deletes the membership — coming back needs a fresh invitation. The owner can't be removed.",
  "help_analytics_title": "Analytics",
  "help_analytics_1Title": "Charts and statistics",
  "help_analytics_1Body": "Planning progress, cost structure and attendance. A good place to check whether the budget is drifting away from the plan.",
  "help_settings_title": "Settings and data",
  "help_settings_1Title": "Wedding configuration",
  "help_settings_1Body": "Name, date, time, ceremony and reception venues, the cost split and the dictionaries (menu, expense categories). After changing the date or the surnames, save the configuration — that refreshes the guest joining details.",
  "help_settings_2Title": "Sync",
  "help_settings_2Body": "Data is saved in the cloud and shared by everyone organising the wedding. The status card sits at the top of Settings.",
  "help_settings_3Title": "Backups and export",
  "help_settings_3Body": "You can create a backup and export all your data to a JSON file. Importing overwrites the wedding's data — handle with care.",
  "help_settings_4Title": "App lock",
  "help_settings_4Body": "A PIN, a pattern or biometrics protect access on this device. The setting is local — it doesn't carry over to other phones.",
  "help_planner_title": "Working with clients",
  "help_planner_1Title": "Several weddings on one account",
  "help_planner_1Body": "You can run as many weddings as you like. Switch between them in the menu under the logo → „Switch wedding\". Each wedding's data is fully separated — client A never sees client B's wedding.",
  "help_planner_2Title": "Your access may be time-limited",
  "help_planner_2Body": "The couple can grant you access with an expiry date, and block or restore it. When a wedding disappears from your list it's usually an expired date rather than a fault — ask your client to extend it.",
  "help_planner_3Title": "What a planner cannot do",
  "help_planner_3Body": "Adding people and issuing invitations is reserved for the wedding's owner. That's deliberate: the client always controls who has access to their data.",
  "help_planner_4Title": "Handing the wedding over to the couple",
  "help_planner_4Body": "There's no separate „handover\" — the wedding belongs to the couple from the start. When your work together ends you simply lose access and all the data stays with the client. Nothing needs exporting.",
  "help_planner_5Title": "Clients' personal data",
  "help_planner_5Body": "The guest list holds personal data: surnames, phone numbers, e-mail addresses, dietary information. Treat it as confidential and never move it between weddings.",
  "help_planner_6Title": "What to show the client",
  "help_planner_6Body": "These usually work best: the Budget summary (where the money goes), the seating plan (printed) and the running order. Analytics gives you a ready-made progress report.",
  "help_gStart_title": "First things first",
  "help_gStart_1Title": "What this page is",
  "help_gStart_1Body": "This is the guest zone put together by the couple. You don't need an account and there's nothing to install — the link or QR code from the invitation is enough.",
  "help_gStart_2Title": "I can't see one of the sections",
  "help_gStart_2Body": "The couple decide what to share and when. Some sections appear only closer to the wedding, and some disappear afterwards. Check back later.",
  "help_gRsvp_title": "Confirming attendance",
  "help_gRsvp_1Title": "How to confirm",
  "help_gRsvp_1Body": "Open RSVP, enter your first and last name, say whether you're coming and send it. If someone's coming with you, give the number of companions — don't fill the form in a second time on their behalf.",
  "help_gRsvp_2Title": "Changing your answer",
  "help_gRsvp_2Body": "One reply is enough. If your plans change, go back to RSVP — the form fills in with your previous answer, and saving replaces it with the new one.",
  "help_gRsvp_3Title": "Diet and allergies",
  "help_gRsvp_3Body": "Enter them on the RSVP form. That goes straight to the couple and helps them agree the menu with the venue.",
  "help_gPhotos_title": "Photos",
  "help_gPhotos_1Title": "Adding photos",
  "help_gPhotos_1Body": "In the Gallery, enter your name and pick a photo from your phone or take one there and then. You can add a caption. There's no limit on how many photos you add.",
  "help_gPhotos_2Title": "Who sees my photos",
  "help_gPhotos_2Body": "The gallery is shared — every guest with the link sees it, and so do the couple. They can delete any photo.",
  "help_gMusic_title": "Music",
  "help_gMusic_1Title": "Suggesting a song",
  "help_gMusic_1Body": "Search for a song, or type the title and artist in yourself, then send the suggestion. If the search doesn't work (it sometimes doesn't in a browser), use the manual fields — the result is the same.",
  "help_gMusic_2Title": "Who sees the suggestions",
  "help_gMusic_2Body": "Only the couple. There's no public list and no voting, so nobody can see what anyone else suggested.",
  "help_gSchedule_title": "Schedule",
  "help_gSchedule_1Title": "Running order",
  "help_gSchedule_1Body": "Hour by hour: the ceremony, the reception, the cake, the first dance. At the top you'll find a countdown to the wedding.",
  "help_gGames_title": "Games",
  "help_gGames_1Title": "Quiz, True/False, Guess the photo",
  "help_gGames_1Body": "Answer every question and send your score. You can have another go — the new score replaces the old one, so you lose nothing.",
  "help_gGames_2Title": "Photo challenges",
  "help_gGames_2Body": "A list of photo tasks. You send one photo per challenge; a new one replaces the old. All guests see the photos.",
  "help_gGames_3Title": "Wedding Bingo",
  "help_gGames_3Body": "Cross squares off as you spot them at the wedding. The crosses stay on your phone — only send your entry once you have a full set.",
  "help_gGames_4Title": "Who sees the scores",
  "help_gGames_4Body": "The couple, and nobody else. There's no public ranking, so play for fun rather than to compete.",
  "help_gKeepsakes_title": "Keepsakes",
  "help_gKeepsakes_1Title": "Guest book and advice",
  "help_gKeepsakes_1Body": "Leave your wishes or a piece of good advice for the couple. You can add several entries, and other guests see them too — it's a shared chronicle of sorts.",
  "help_gKeepsakes_2Title": "Time capsule",
  "help_gKeepsakes_2Body": "A private message to the couple. No other guest will see it.",
  "help_gKeepsakes_3Title": "Guest map",
  "help_gKeepsakes_3Body": "Mark where you're travelling from. One pin per guest — you can correct it by coming back to the section.",
  "help_gPrivacy_title": "Privacy",
  "help_gPrivacy_1Title": "What the couple see",
  "help_gPrivacy_1Body": "Your RSVP, your entries, photos, music suggestions and game scores — always with the name you give.",
  "help_gPrivacy_2Title": "What other guests don't see",
  "help_gPrivacy_2Body": "Your RSVP, your time capsule message, your music suggestions and your game scores. Only these are public: the guest book, advice, the map, the gallery and photo-challenge pictures.",
  "setupTask_eventNameLabel": "Wedding name",
  "setupTask_eventNameHint": "E.g. „Anna and Peter's Wedding\" — it appears in the app header and on the guest page.",
  "setupTask_weddingDateLabel": "Wedding date and time",
  "setupTask_weddingDateHint": "The date drives the dashboard countdown and the guest verification when someone joins with a code.",
  "setupTask_coupleTypeLabel": "Type of celebration",
  "setupTask_coupleTypeHint": "Decides the labels across the whole app — „Bride / Groom\", two brides, two grooms, or neutral wording.",
  "setupTask_coupleNamesLabel": "The couple's first names",
  "setupTask_coupleNamesHint": "Enter both names — the cost split, the labels and the guest list all use them.",
  "setupTask_ceremonyPlaceLabel": "Ceremony venue",
  "setupTask_ceremonyPlaceHint": "The church or registry office — guests see the address in the schedule.",
  "setupTask_receptionPlaceLabel": "Reception venue",
  "setupTask_receptionPlaceHint": "The venue's name and address — this reaches the guest schedule too.",
  "setupTask_verificationSurnamesLabel": "Surname for guest verification",
  "setupTask_verificationSurnamesHint": "The surname (or both surnames) a guest enters when joining with a code. It's never displayed anywhere — it only serves the check.",
  "setupTask_guestsLabel": "First guests",
  "setupTask_guestsHint": "Add at least a few people — catering, tables and statistics all depend on the guest list.",
  "setupTask_budgetTotalLabel": "Planned budget",
  "setupTask_budgetTotalHint": "The figure you want to stay within. Without it there's nothing to compare your spending against.",
  "setupTask_pricePerPersonLabel": "Price per person (venue)",
  "setupTask_pricePerPersonHint": "The per-plate rate — multiplied by the number of guests to give the catering cost.",
  "setupTask_withChildrenLabel": "Decision about children",
  "setupTask_withChildrenHint": "Decide whether children will attend. If they will, you get a children's menu, a children's table, and they're left out of the drinks calculations.",
  "setupTask_menuOptionsLabel": "Menu dictionary",
  "setupTask_menuOptionsHint": "The meal options to pick from for each guest (meat, fish, vegetarian, children's).",
  "setupTask_expenseCategoriesLabel": "Expense categories",
  "setupTask_expenseCategoriesHint": "Your own cost categories — expenses and the Analytics charts are grouped by them.",
  "setupTask_witnessesLabel": "Witnesses",
  "setupTask_witnessesHint": "Mark the witnesses on the guest list — they'll show up in the summary and on the seating plan.",
  "setupTask_tablesLabel": "Tables",
  "setupTask_tablesHint": "Add tables with their number of seats — without them you can't seat anyone.",
  "setupTask_seatingLabel": "Seating guests",
  "setupTask_seatingHint": "Assign guests to tables — even just some of them. You'll finish the rest closer to the wedding.",
  "setupTask_scheduleLabel": "Running order",
  "setupTask_scheduleHint": "Programme items with times. Guests see this same schedule in their zone.",
  "setupTask_guestVisibilityLabel": "Section visibility for guests",
  "setupTask_guestVisibilityHint": "Decide what guests see and from when — e.g. RSVP right away, the gallery only on the wedding day.",
  "setupLevel_basic": "Basic setup",
  "setupLevel_advanced": "Advanced setup",
  "setupLevel_basicIntro": "The minimum to get going: the wedding details and your first guests.",
  "setupLevel_advancedIntro": "The finishing touches: budget, menu, tables, schedule and the guest zone. Anything you've already filled in is ticked off.",
